  :seon.task/proofs #{my.schema-test/a-key-a-second-file-defines-is-refused-naming-both-files}}
 {:seon.task/name "deps-edn-and-pins-are-edited-on-the-branch"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: deps. Root, 2026-11-15 (owner's ruling: every edit through the branch and its merge): context's place list (seon.ctx/every-session-works-as-a-seon-agent-does, item 12) has no place for deps.edn or the pins, so a dependency change is a file edit outside the branch. PRIOR WORK (git grep src for seon.pin, pins-of, file-kinds, file-kind, write-back!, :git effect): the pins are already facts on a branch (:seon.pin/pin-fact, schemas/seon.facts.edn:105-107), written by the import from the tree's gitlinks (seon.source/pin-changes-tx :321, pins-of :314, the import :346-350), and read by the runtime's identity; a file kind is one row of seon.source's file-kinds table (source.clj:300: {:tx :text}), chosen by seon.config/file-kind over :seon.config.source/things (config.clj:483), which edit!, the import, the merge and the write-back all read; the write-back (my.root/write-back!, root.clj:187) commits through the one :git effect, which takes :files and :modes only, so no path writes a pin back to git. DESIGN, no new mechanism: (1) deps.edn becomes a file kind: a :seon.config.source/things entry and a file-kinds row like :script's ({:tx file facts :text held-text}), so edit! on it, the merge and the write-back carry it as every file. (2) a pin is edited as the fact it already is: (my.branch/pin! path commit) transacts seon.source/pin-changes-tx on the agent's branch (the commit checked to exist in the submodule's repository first, a typed error when not); the merge carries it as any fact; the :git effect gains :pins {path commit}, the pins main holds that the tree does not (pins-of against the tree's gitlinks), written in the same commit by git update-index --cacheinfo 160000,COMMIT,PATH. The fork's own commits stay where they are made (the fork's jolt/<topic> branch, pushed); the pin names one. COST: a pin edit one fact; the write-back one update-index a moved pin inside the commit it already makes; deps.edn as any file. A pin or deps.edn change is a build input, so the landing's identity check (seon.fx/runtime-for) says build, as today. Proofs, red first: seon.source-test/a-pin-edited-on-a-branch-reaches-mains-gitlink (an agent's pin! merged, written back: the tree's gitlink at that commit); seon.source-test/deps-edn-is-edited-on-the-branch (edit! on deps.edn merged and written back). Needs the identity fix (seon.program/a-process-runs-its-branchs-program, deps' rev 2) on main first, so a pin's merge is judged by one identity."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.source-test/a-pin-edited-on-a-branch-reaches-mains-gitlink seon.source-test/deps-edn-is-edited-on-the-branch}
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.program/a-process-runs-its-branchs-program"}
  :seon.task/estimate #:seon.source{pin-changes-tx {:n 50, :order :linear, :ticks 50000, :bytes 20000}}}
 {:seon.task/name "importing-a-task-file-keeps-the-branch-the-system-set", :seon.task/kind :work, :seon.task/proofs #{seon.source-test/import-then-write-back-is-a-zero-diff}, :seon.task/estimate {seon.source/import-tx {:n 1, :order :linear, :ticks 1000000, :bytes 5000000}}, :seon.task/plan "Owner: whoever owns seon.source's task import (seon.source). Found by data, 2026-11-16 [M root result/c8aae1e3]: landing d3a8060230 changed one task's file entry (seon.db/an-eval-responses-parts-are-its-schemas-keys); its import (tx 536910328) moved that task's :seon.task/branch back from :task-seon-db-an-eval-responses-parts-are-its-schemas-keys-r536905006, which the system set when a fresh attach moved the task (seon.task/restart-tx), to the default :task-seon-db-an-eval-responses-parts-are-its-schemas-keys; the next seon_attach spawned an agent on the old empty branch, and the pilot's work was out of reach until a repair. :seon.task/branch is state the system writes, never file content, so an import of a task's file entry leaves it (and every attribute the file does not state) as main holds it. The proof to write, red first: a task moved to a fresh branch keeps that branch when its file entry is imported again; its proof extends seon.source-test/import-then-write-back-is-a-zero-diff."}

 {:seon.task/name "a-reviewed-syncs-fix-reaches-the-merges-branch"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by data landing the pilot sync 7875387c3e, 2026-11-16 05:4x: root's review fixed the sync branch (97ac6cf112, comments moved in seon.core.edn) after the agent's write-back had committed the unfixed file on jolt/merges (85cc745c06); the land's update then could not merge main into .worktrees/merges (conflict on resources/seon/schemas/seon.core.edn, aborted) and every update stops there until it is resolved [land log target/land/*-jolt-data.log, UPDATE FAILED]. The class: a reviewed sync's fix is a second writer of a file the write-back already committed. PRIOR WORK: my.root/sync! and sync-req (docs/source.md#a-merged-task-reaches-mains-files), my.root/merges-caught-up! (the :git effect's {:merge}), seon.fx/merge-in-tree!. Fix at the data: a sync's files on jolt/merges are main's once the sync lands (the store's main holds the reviewed text after the bridge), so the update's merge takes main's side for the files a landed sync names (its Completes: tasks' changed paths), and a conflict on any other file still stops it. Root resolved it by hand, 2026-11-16 05:5x: merged main in .worktrees/merges and took main's seon.core.edn whole (git -X theirs alone left duplicate :fns/:bytes/:ns/:repaired entries), jolt/merges 6bd14e43be with main's tree: a by-hand merge outside the :git effect, the tree's one writer, which this fix makes unneeded. Watch: until an update's merges-caught-up! moves main's source :commit to jolt/merges' head, a write-back's compare-and-swap refuses (the fact named fd2af47045). COST: one read of the landed commits' Completes: lines an update (seon.task/completes, already read by landed-completes)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.source-test/an-update-takes-mains-side-for-a-landed-syncs-files}
